 "text": "Hi, how are you doing right now? He' need a good walking stick or small backpack with a light tower at each landing. A guide can do it with a quick eye. Then go together and accept it as it is. You can pack a bag each landing and leave at a nice moment, like at the bottom after shopping. Some people do, but it' not safe for everyone. Keep the weight down and take fast steps one step at a time. Offer him the lift bowl on the way out, and try to go together during the day when there's no night noises to compare it with. He' get used to it, it just takes a little bit of respect.",
